  "id": "equivalency-test",
  "term": "equivalency test",
  "definition": "An equivalency test is a statistical test used to show that repeated measurements or different raters are similar enough to be considered practically the same within preset limits. In this study, it tested whether the confidence intervals for differences in repeated measures stayed inside an a priori equivalence range, allowing rejection of non-equivalence.",
